{
 "_doc": "The Spriggan (Hunt, 1865; Bottrell, 1870-73: the treasure guard who can swell to a giant's size): an ugly, knotted grey-brown fairy, hunched and lumpy, with a big head, a huge hooked nose, small glowing eyes, pointed ears, wild hair like roots, a wide snaggle-toothed grin, very long arms with knobbly hands, short bandy legs, a ragged mossy tunic and a pouch of gold at his belt; small in his own shape and huge when swollen. Built by tools/art/build_otherworlds.py.",
